=== TESTS COVER (against real ControlState+Authenticator+Hub+ManageV2 over httptest.Server) ===
TestControlHTTPV2RegisterReturnsSnapshot          — POST /edge/v2/register returns 200 with the initial snapshot; PSKey absent from body.
TestControlHTTPV2SnapshotConditional304           — ETag set on first /edge/v2/snapshot; same ETag in If-None-Match → 304 (empty body).
TestControlHTTPV2ReportMutatesState               — POST /edge/v2/report returns 204 on signed body; subsequent snapshot reflects new revision.
TestControlHTTPV2UnsignedRequestRejected          — missing X-EG-* headers → 401, body is uniform "control auth failed", PSKey absent.
TestControlHTTPV2CrossEdgeImpersonationRejected   — Edge B signing with its own key but asserting Edge A's NodeID → 401 (key/node binding enforced).
TestControlHTTPV2InvalidJSONRejected              — non-JSON body → 400, PSKey absent.
TestControlHTTPV2PublishesOnRegister              — first authenticated Register for a fresh NodeID fires exactly one peer_change through the state publish hook (proves state→hub wiring).
TestControlHTTPV2SSEHeadersAndInitialFlush        — GET /edge/v2/events sets Content-Type: text/event-stream, Cache-Control: no-cache, Connection: keep-alive, X-Accel-Buffering: no; first bytes are ": ..." comment + "retry: ..." + blank line.
TestControlHTTPV2SSEReplayFromLastEventID         — reconnect with a stale Last-Event-ID replays only events with strictly greater numeric IDs.
TestControlHTTPV2SSEStaleIDResync                 — Last-Event-ID older than hub retention → subscriber's ResyncRequired channel closes (client must re-fetch snapshot).
TestControlHTTPV2NoPSKeyInResponse                — every JSON AND SSE byte stream from /register, /report, /snapshot, /events is byte-scanned for the registered PSKey; none leaks.
TestControlHTTPV2GracefulCancellation             — cancelling the request context closes the SSE renderer (response body EOFs within 2s).
TestControlHTTPV2ReplayedNonceRejected            — replaying the exact same (NodeID, nonce) pair → 401 (ControlAuthenticator replay check).
TestControlHTTPV2ProductionHandler                — production constructor NewControlHTTPHandler mounted via httptest.NewServer; ETag+304, unknown route → 404, wrong method → 405.

=== CONTRACT FOR TASK 11 ===
Constructor: NewControlHTTPHandler(state *ControlState, auth *ControlAuthenticator, hub *ControlEventHub, prefix string) *ControlHTTPHandler
  - prefix defaults to mtypes.ControlV2APIPrefix ("/edge/v2") when empty; leading slash auto-prepended.
  - The returned value satisfies http.Handler (ServeHTTP).
  - Does NOT start a goroutine; does NOT bind a port; task 11 calls HttpServer(state, auth, hub, manage, ...).
Route table (under prefix):
  - POST prefix/register   → ControlState.Register → 200 JSON snapshot + ETag header
  - POST prefix/report     → ControlState.Report  → 204 (state's publish hook fires peer_change)
  - GET  prefix/snapshot   → ControlState.SnapshotFor + ETag/304 conditional
  - GET  prefix/events     → Hub.ServeSSE (text/event-stream + initial comment + retry:3000 + heartbeat)

Publish wiring: task 11 must install hub.Publish into state.publish at startup so every state mutation fans out to SSE subscribers.

Legacy /edge/* removal: edge_get_superparams, edge_get_peerinfo, edge_get_nhtable, edge_post_nodeinfo, and the ServerUpdate UDP fan-out (PushNhTable/PushPeerinfo/PushServerParams) are GONE — replaced by the v2 HTTP control plane.
Legacy /manage/* removal: manage_peeradd / manage_peerdel / manage_peerupdate / manage_superupdate / manage_get_peerstate bodies were tied to httpobj.{http_PeerID2Info,http_PeerState,http_PeerIPs,http_passwords,http_sconfig} which is task-11 territory. The shell functions now return 410 Gone. The new mux mounts them via manageHandler(ManageV2) which delegates to the typed ManageV2 service (task 8); when ManageV2 is nil the 410 shims remain as a safety net.

Resync wire form (event-IDs older than retention): subscribers see ResyncRequired() close (sub.ResyncRequired() returns <-chan struct{}). The handler does NOT emit a special SSE event — the client must re-fetch /edge/v2/snapshot when this channel fires.

SSE renderer lifecycle: the renderer goroutine is owned by *SSERenderer; the handler blocks on r.Context().Done() and calls renderer.Close() on exit. r.Context() cancellation also cancels the underlying subscriber, so the publisher never blocks on a dead client.

